  "scientific_conclusions": {
    "block_balanced_sft": "Supported: independently averaging score and rationale fields and then weighting the two task blocks prevents the longer rationale field from dominating the SFT objective. It outperforms global token averaging on MAE, Exact and Kendall; its L2H improvement is directional after primary-family correction.",
    "field_local_dpo": "Supported: applying preference learning to the intended score field is better than applying ordinary full-sequence DPO to the same preference records.",
    "actual_error_negatives": "Supported: negatives derived from frozen R3-SFT errors outperform record-matched synthetic score negatives under the frozen comparison.",
    "overall": "The mechanism controls close the main attribution gap: the gains are associated with block-balanced SFT supervision, field-local preference optimization and actual-error-driven negatives, rather than with generic extra SFT or generic DPO alone."
  },
